claim.claim-text:
a body that defines a duct (101) with an upper end and a lower end opposite the upper end, the duct (101) has a diameter that flares at the lower end;
at least one electric motor (107) controlled by an electronic controller;
at least one fan (108) operatively coupled to the at least one electric motor for rotating the at least one fan (108) and creating an airflow into the upper end of the duct (101) and out the lower end of the duct (101) which creates thrust; and
one or more flaps (106) installed on the body and configured to redirect the airflow at the lower end of the duct (101) by protruding into the airflow.
